NAME
    ps - list running processes

SYNOPSIS
    ps
    ps --json
    ps --advjson

DESCRIPTION
    Shows every user task currently in the task table. Default
    output is a column-aligned table with PID, PPID, STATE, NAME.

    Kernel-only tasks (kmain, the reaper, demo tasks) are filtered
    out — only is_user=1 tasks are listed.

    --advjson (session 81) emits one JSONL record per task with
    fields: pid, ppid, state, name, uid, gid, rss_pages, cpu_ticks,
    limits (nested object with rss/cpu/wall/fds caps), sandbox
    (bitmask of installed syscall masks).

EXAMPLES
    ps
    ps |> where state=RUNNING
    ps |> sort -k pid |> head -5

EXIT STATUS
    0   listing emitted
    1   no tasks visible (should not happen — kmain is always there)

SEE ALSO
    kill(1), id(1), ls(1)

NOTES
    The state field is one of: READY, RUNNING, BLOCKED, ZOMBIE,
    DEAD, STOPPED, BLOCKED_ON_CHILD. See kernel/task.h for the
    full enum.
